<<~ kanawai uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119`>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The Session Contract ~ what a tab or a CLI run holds, and what it never holds

''A session wears the face and the vessel wears none'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy#/the-session`>>). This carrier states the contract under that ruling: what a session carries, what the vessel's owner keeps for it, how a surface mounts, how the holder speaks, and how a session switches and ends.

''One vessel holds one durable backing Repo, one store lock, custody, and one trusted, face-blind daemon.'' Each tab or CLI run opens a volatile session that wears exactly one verified face. The gate-facing half of the same ruling, the proof a session presents on the wire, stands at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof`>>.

> ''Register.'' The operator approved this contract's decisions as presented (operator ruling, 2026-10-11; quote license: //"Pono, this all reads good. Flowstate approved (per tab state reads pono, we want that, and can sync up 'views' later if needed)."//). A sentence below that carries the operator's own words stands as law. The remainder reads as ''the designed shape'': approved in outline, and unbuilt wherever #/standing-and-owed says OWED. One reading belongs to the house and carries its own mark (#/receipts).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/what-a-session-carries`>>

!! What a session carries ~ an id that routes, a binding that authorizes

|! Field |! What it holds |! What it never holds |
| `sessionId` | a fresh random handle the owner mints; it ROUTES a message to its session | authority: a copied id opens nothing |
| `ownerEpoch` | the owner's own boot epoch, a fresh random mint at each boot; it fences a restarted holder | a wall-clock reading, or a counter derived from one |
| `generation` | a counter that advances at a switch; an effect of an earlier generation never lands in a later one | |
| `face` | the resolved face, immutable within one generation: the PersonaGroup, its proof subject, its verified admit, the causal revision the relation stood at, and the absolute ids of its four planes (`@persona` · `@circles` · `@identities` · `@sessions`) | a persona root, or any root bytes |
| `caps` | operation facets the sovereign worker holds for this session | a Repo, a root, or a signer map |
| `state` | `opening` · `live` · `switching` · `revoked` · `closing` · `closed` | |
| `surfaces` | each mounted surface with the island it leases | |

''The id routes; the binding and the worker-held capabilities authorize.'' The sovereign worker verifies custody or delegation, the admit, the proof subject, the plane derivation and the relation's observed state. The owner then mints the id and binds it to the pending port or socket. Every later message gets checked against that binding before it routes, and the worker checks the bound facet and the verb.

''A socket or port binds five things'': the owner epoch, the session id, the generation, a verified face reference (the face's proof subject) and a fixed hand profile. `SessionTable.checkBound` reads a bound message in one order: a malformed envelope, a stale owner epoch, an unknown session, an id presented on a binding other than the one that opened it (`unbound-session`: a copied socket), a stale generation, a face reference other than the session's proof subject (`wrong-face`), a session not live. A refusal never mutates the table, and `bound` answers the five parts as references alone.

''A session never receives a Repo, a root, or a signer map.'' It receives handles to bounded operations, and the daemon invokes each one on its behalf.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-hands`>>

!! The hands ~ every hand opens a session, and hands differ by profile, never by key

''Every hand that reaches a vessel opens a session, and a session wears one face'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-12, approved as presented). A hand names WHO moved; the face names the relation the move speaks in. Hands differ by capability profile. No hand holds a key, and no second kind of identity stands beside the face.

|! Hand |! Its session |! Its profile |
| a person in a live wiki | a tab | the face's own |
| a person at the CLI | a CLI run (#/the-cli) | the verb's |
| the disk | the watcher, a session that leases each projected wiki as a surface | ingest for the wikis it leases |
| a spirit | an MCP connection: the seat | narrower than the face's; its writes land in the working layer, and reach a bag only by a person's residency move |

''A spirit holds a seat and no key'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-12; quote license: //"the spirit's identity enacts the operator's relationship"//; //"you all get a 'seat' here in the lararium … your persona's don't trade keys out, the vessel itself serves as your identity-as-relation across all AI frontier model providers and locally run models later"//). The seat rests on the vessel. A model from any provider, or a model run locally, may sit in it, and none carries it away. A spirit's persona names who authored; it never names who signed.

''A tasked spirit comes down to an AI, a Mask and the vessel's seat'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-12; quote license: //"I consider you an extention of my hands, that's Identity as Relation right there"//; //"tasked spirits are just AI, they carry pet-names and the vessel seat"//, where the operator's loose word names what this house writes as a Mask). The seat belongs to the vessel and never to a spirit. Two positions stand in it.

|! Position |! When |! Who signs |! What another party sees |
| ''attended'' | the operator sits in the session and directs the work: the spirit extends the operator's hands | the operator's face, as the operator's own act | the operator's act, with the spirit's Mask as authorship |
| ''standing'' | a spirit works under a standing grant, with no person in the loop | nothing that changes who holds authority; it drafts | working-layer writes carrying a Mask |

''The vessel's own key serves as a spirit's system identity.'' No spirit holds a key of its own, and the house mints none for it. A model from any provider sits in the same seat, and an act that crosses a vessel presents what any session of that face on that vessel presents (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof`>>). The operator answers for a spirit's acts: a neighbour who shadows the spirit shadows that vessel's edge. A derived lineage handle addresses and recalls a spirit's work and grants no identity (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/agent-worldline`>> · <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/mandate-activity-provenance`>>).

* ''A standing grant names the face a seat wears.'' The grant rests at the MCP mount. The owner verifies it afresh at every open, and it opens nothing while the vessel rests at the floor: no spirit works on a locked vessel.
* ''The Mask travels as authorship.'' A write into a shared realm carries the hand that made it as a field of the record, beside the face that signs: the kind of hand, and a spirit's Mask. The field names and authorizes nothing; no gate reads it. A Mask pins to no key and no identifier, so it counts as no pet-name (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy`>>).
* ''An agent's dissent drafts; a person's ask edits'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). An agent that disagrees with a person's edit files its own version as a draft beside it, and the person's edit stands until the person chooses: an agent never overrides. A person who asks an agent to edit a tiddler directly makes that edit the person's own act (the ''attended'' position above), and the agent writes it, reaching only the tiddlers the ask names and only under the asker's own write authority.
* ''A projected wiki stands as a surface.'' One tree on disk serves the person. A wiki names a face's relation to a composition (#/the-working-layer), so each face's wiki takes its own folder and the path says whose wiki it holds. No file and no `.meta` chooses the signer: an edit returns under the face of the session that leases the surface. A switch advances the generation, and an edit sensed under an earlier generation surfaces as a draft.
* ''Files that changed while no session held the lease'' ingest at the next mount, under the mounting face, as surfaced drafts.

''The door carries; the hand authorizes'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-12, approved as presented). MCP and the CLI stand as two doors onto one contract: the same session messages over the one socket, one verb table, the same named refusals, the same receipts. Parity belongs to the doors. A profile belongs to the hand, and no door widens or narrows it.

* ''One verb table serves every hand.'' A seat sees every verb, and a verb beyond its profile refuses by name. OWED to the hands room's profile lane: the node seat checks a session's face and anchor on `session:call` and `session:act`, never its profile, so a `watcher` or `tab` session runs a face row or `host.roll` as its face until the profile-verb table gates both (its red: such a call refuses by profile; a seat's session runs it).
* ''A seat never signs an act that changes who holds authority'' (an attended spirit acts as the operator, so this bound falls on a standing one alone): a vault or custody verb, an admit, a kapae, a quorum signature, a face switch, or a residency move into a bag. A seat MAY draft such an act for a person to sign.
* ''Authority only narrows down a chain of spirits.'' A spirit MAY seat a sub-spirit under a profile no wider than its own, and the Mask records the chain.
* ''A container makes the profile bind.'' A spirit that shares its operator's OS account reaches every door that operator reaches, and its declared hand stays a declaration. A spirit that runs in a container holding only its seat's socket and grant holds no other door.

''A session switches in place, and the door reads afresh.'' A session's switch runs the five-step fence over its own table entry: freeze and preflight, the intent, the fence of the outgoing generation, advance and commit, the outcome and then live. A commit that fails closes that session alone, and a sibling session of the same face keeps its generation, face and signer. The node's production door (`packages/lararium-node/src/uds-session-door.ts`) takes an `h<N>` hint, reads that face's anchors, its K15 atom (the presenter) and its proof at the Nexus the vessel dials, and reads and writes nothing; a locked face refuses `face-locked`, any other fault `door-failed` with its detail kept in the vessel's log, and a proof of another PersonaGroup `face-group-mismatch`. ''A session is a meeting between a face and an anchor, held by neither's registry'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-27): identity-as-relation for places as for faces. One session binds one (face, anchor). The anchor is the Nexus the vessel dials, or, for a vessel standing with no Nexus, the vessel's own place, named by its W29 place KEL prefix; the vessel's state decides which (a dial pin standing, or none), never its config. At a place anchor the face proves itself by its atom presented to its own vessel, with no Nexus admit. A proof at another anchor refuses `anchor-moved`, and every command that acts as a face rides a session of that face on a running vessel; rows and acts of the place keep their frames, and verbs that run with no vessel open stay off sessions. Built: each supply names its anchor, `{ kind: "nexus", aid }` or `{ kind: "place", aid: <W29 place KEL prefix>, head }`, and the door answers `anchorNow`, reading where the place KEL stands at each check (its login read once, so a git config change moves no anchor, and a verify only once the KEL's bytes moved), so a rotation of the place moves the anchor and a read that fails refuses that one frame `anchor-unread` with the session standing; the place signer reads the same head before and after each signature, so a rotation between a frame's check and the signature refuses `anchor-moved` there; the dial pin stands only once the vessel's own presentation composed at it, so a refused composition or a failed re-dial leaves the vessel at its place anchor. At the place the door supplies the face from its atom and the place alone (`supplyPlaceFace`: the proof subject names the atom and the place, the admit reference the place KEL's head) and the atom certifies the session's key (`PlaceSessionSigner`, under four place domains apart from every Nexus image). A session whose anchor the vessel left ends `anchor-moved` at its next frame, and a switch whose proof stands at another anchor refuses `anchor-moved`. Every store-door row that acts as a face (`STORE_DOOR_FACE_ROWS`) rides a session of that face on a running vessel, and the maintenance frame refuses such a row `face-row-rides-a-session`; rows of the place keep the frame. ''A face row's answer rides the socket alone'' (`K20`): each rides `session:act`, where the vessel's main thread runs it as the face the session wears once the keyholder island clears it as it clears a routed verb (`daemon:gate-verb-request`, nothing placed or dispatched), its answer returns on that socket, and its receipt names the act and the face; a `session:call`, whose outcome body rests in the daemon document beside the session's face, refuses a face row `answers-on-the-socket`. The realm verbs that name a face's key at a realm's Nexus (`REALM_KEY_VERBS`: `realm-bag`, which signs as the worn face, `realm-bags` and `realm-clock`) refuse a call the same way: `realm-bag` and `realm-bags` ride `session:act` as the session's face, and `realm-clock` rides the maintenance frame, which names no face. ''The session's face binds what it carries'': the supply names the face's ordinal, and a row whose `face` or `handleIndex` names another face, or whose two keys disagree, refuses `face-row-other-face`, never overwritten; a row naming none acts as the session's face. Every sealed act that signs, reads or writes as a face (`SESSION_ACTS`: persona.reissue, walk.take, host.roll, crossing.sign, crossing.witness, carriage.accept, persona.recovery-contact.enrol, persona.confirm, handle-book.load, handle-book.save, selves.carry, selves.clear) rides `session:act` on the custody door's one chain under the same binding, naming its face by its own key (`face`, else `handleIndex` for the acts keyed by it alone), and the receipt each leaves names the act and the face alone, never an argument or the answer; a retry under one requestId reads that receipt, the act running once per id and its answer never surviving a hang-up. ''One requestId, one intent'' (the retry contract): the receipt's digest covers the act and the face and never an argument, so a caller that reuses an id for other arguments reads the first act's receipt and its new intent never runs; a caller draws a fresh id for each intent and reuses one only to retry that same intent. A ledger that fails before the run answers `session-fault` (nothing ran); a ledger that fails to record the outcome after the run answers `act-faulted` with the receipt, never `session-fault`, and a retry under that id reads the act's outcome, never `pending`; the custody door's own act frame refuses them `face-act-rides-a-session`. Every other sealed act acts as the place and stays at the custody door (the lane kit names each and why); `face.resolve` among them reads and signs nothing, and cannot ride the session it chooses, and `persona.view` signs as a held chair, never as a face. A restored face standing provisional opens a session like any other, so its confirm rides one. The seal roll anchors by authority: the acting face's session proves it opens before any card reads, the carriage anchor rides the frame as the place's row and gates the roll, and each realm edge anchor rides a session of the face named or resolved after the charter lands, never halving the roll: with no face open the edge step answers `no-face-open`, and a face that locked after the preflight leaves the edge anchors `owed` by name. A daemon that boots one face's Keyhive provider judges a second face's session as the stranger its atom reads as, until the next lane routes each session to its face's own provider. A hint naming a Nexus (`h<N>@<aid>`) waits on a vessel that dials a second Nexus.

* ''The daemon holds one Keyhive provider per joined face'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-27; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k19-hive-lane`>>). Each unlocked face boots through the full gate over its own cap-event scope and bag-document ledger, and a verify routes by the session's presenter atom: an atom no provider holds refuses "no provider for face <key>", and the place key gets no grant. No verifier judges many faces. A sibling's lock and unlock ride `daemon:face-drop` and `daemon:face-lit` and recompose nothing.
* ''A session acts only as the face it wears.'' The UDS session door places each session ask with its face's ordinal, and the vessel's main thread books that face (ordinal and verified presenter) by request id as it places the ask; a delegate back from the island hands its handler that booking, never the presenter the delegate names, and a booking serves one delegate of the act it booked, which alone spends it; since `K20` a booking lends a session call its presenter and locality alone, since no face row rides a call. Every store-door face row binds to the face its session wears, which main hands it (`DaemonVmCore.runAsFace`): a row that rode no session refuses `face-row-rides-a-session`, a row naming another face refuses `face-row-other-face`, and a row naming none acts as the worn face, with no fallback to the one face open or to face 0. A row that reads a face acts as that face wherever it sat, so the intent-relay rows `intent-relay-enable`, `-disable` and `-status` are face rows, while the relay key's rotation stays a place row. A realm feed runs on the vessel's main thread as the session's face, bound by the face→leaf bond (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k19-hive-lane`>>), so no answer pairs a face with its leaf. No daemon outcome names its requester (`K20`): the volatile invocation carries who asked, so the realm feed's outcome never names the atom beside the slot its leaf names, and a census (`censusOutcomeLinkage`) reads the daemon outcomes for any that pairs a requester with a key or answers a face row.
* ''A switch act rests on its vessel alone.'' The intent and the outcome name two faces together, and the face's working layer syncs to every vessel of the face's fleet, so they rest in the vessel's sealed `switch-acts` custody row and in no document.
* ''The hand's claim names a profile, and the socket's file mode gates who may claim.'' A `session:open` names its hand; the door grants that hand's profile to whatever process the socket's file mode admits.

> ''Two house readings, marked as such.'' A file moved by hand between two faces' folders arrives as a copy under the destination's face, asked for by name, and never as a silent change of signer. And the house publishes this limit: //facets on one operator's disk hold separate network identities and signing authority; anyone who can inspect that disk or its copies may read their projections and link the facets, and writing style or timing may also link them.//

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-working-layer`>>

!! The working layer ~ one document per face relation, wiki, and slot kind

One working document follows each `(face relation, wiki, slot kind)`. Its address derives from a secret held only by that face's vessels; no binding record or mint race decides the address. Two vessels mounting offline derive one document and merge their writes.

The working layer follows the wiki across recipe recomposition; it never follows the recipe's composition fingerprint. Here, `wiki` names the face's relation to a composition over bags, never a global wiki name or registry id. Two faces at one table may hold wikis that share bags; sharing happens at the bag. Presence and multiplayer spaces sit above shared bags.

A leaf with an admit and no seat writes nothing to the face's wikis. Join first; the face secret arrives at the face-proof join (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-chain`>>).

The gate and document membership refuse a removed vessel. The working document keeps its address; rotation to a fresh document takes a separate, deliberate act.

The working kind resolves through `resolveFaceWorkingSlot` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-working-address.ts`). `faceWorkingDocUrl` derives the address as HMAC-SHA256 under the face's 32-byte address secret over a length-prefixed image of the wiki id and the slot kind, so the recipe's fingerprint never enters it, and `materializeFaceWorkingDoc` finds or materializes the blank pinned document under that id. The resolver refuses `no-address-secret` where the vessel holds no secret for the face, `address-not-derived` where a claimed address differs from the derived one, and a malformed secret, wiki or kind by name; it zero-fills the secret it read and falls back to no device floor. The secret mints at the face's founding, beside its atom and behind its custody, and no read mints one; a face founded before that cut re-founds. The slot-doc resolver (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/slot-doc-resolver.ts`) derives a seated face's working slot by the wiki's slug through a `faceAddressSecret` port the openers serve from main-thread custody, and no record names it. With no face seated the working document keys by the floor's own anchor, read from the vessel and never inferred (`WorkingFloorAnchor`): on a node its place, the W29 place KEL prefix; on a browser leaf, which holds no place KEL, the private Nexus of one it stands as at the floor. It rests in the catalog under that anchor (`wikiWorkingFloorKey`), a vessel holding neither refuses `no-place`, and the anon-veil lift carries it into the face's derived document at the join, after which the anchor's key names nothing. The resolver that keys bindings by `prefix/fingerprint` through `daemonStore` (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/resolve-binding.ts`) serves the draft and personal kinds.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-owner`>>

!! The owner ~ acts and outcomes persist; a roster of sessions never does

''The vessel's owner keeps its live routes in memory alone.'' It persists two things: the switch ACTS, vessel-private, and the durable OUTCOMES of requests. It MUST NOT persist a list of live sessions. A roster of sessions would stand as a record of which faces one vessel wore together, which the session ruling forbids from reaching any wire and which nothing needs at rest.

''A face hint grants nothing.'' A caller may keep the face it last asked for, so a reload asks again; the owner verifies afresh every time.

''The daemon stays face-blind and trusted'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-11: plane isolation inside a vessel runs by capability-limited sessions, and the vessel's own daemon stands trusted). It serves every session, adopts no session's face, and keys its own island by the vessel.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/islands`>>

!! Islands ~ one per interactive surface, and per-tab state as wanted

''Every interactive wiki surface takes its own island.'' The island's key reads `(sessionId, generation, surfaceId, wikiId, facePlaneId, recipeRevision, capabilityProfile)`. A key of wiki and face alone falls short: two tabs wearing one face still carry two writers and two sets of control state.

''Per-tab state stands as the operator wants it'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-11; quote license: //"per tab state reads pono, we want that, and can sync up 'views' later if needed"//). Each tab runs its own TiddlyWiki engine and keeps its own story river, drafts, scroll, cameras and frames. Two tabs of one face share their durable documents through the one owner. Syncing a view across tabs stays a later, optional feature, and nothing in this contract waits on it.

''A camera's frame keys and revisions live within its surface mount'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom#/the-ruling`>>). The pool's bookkeeping, pending calls, failure accounting and leases all use the whole key.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-document-view`>>

!! The session-scoped document view ~ what replaces the broad sync port

''A correctly routed holder protects nothing once an island can fetch any document.'' So a session island never receives unrestricted Repo sync. It receives a ''session-scoped document view'', and that view gates five things: document announcements, fetches, writes, catalog resolution, and content-addressed reads.

''Session islands hold ephemeral replicas; the vessel's owner alone persists.'' No durable per-island store survives a session. A plane address a caller supplies grants nothing: the view answers from the session's own facets.

''The first test of this contract'': ask a session island's sync path for an arbitrary document. One byte of another face's plane, or one catalog name from it, breaks the contract.

''The view rides the carrier.'' A peer names its own id, so a verdict keyed by peer id protects nothing from an island that announces another's. The view mints the island's peer id and judges every message that crosses the island's own port, in both directions; an island that announces any other id loses its channel. A fetch the view refuses answers as absence does, so a refusal tells an island nothing about what stands.

> ''Four house readings, marked as such.'' ''A bag reaches a session read-only'': a session writes its wiki's working, personal and draft layers and its face's own planes, and a move into a bag runs as an owner-side verb, never as an island's sync write. ''One table of profile against layer decides a write'': a seat writes the working layer alone, and the watcher writes the working layer and surfaces drafts. ''Content opens by reference'': a session reads the content its recipe names and the content a document it may read references; the owner's store answers, and bytes that fail to recompute to their address never leave. ''An island settles before it goes'': a session island keeps no store, so at an orderly close it names the heads it holds and waits until the owner holds them; a switch or a revocation closes its channel first.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-effective-recipe`>>

!! The effective recipe ~ one function, at surface mount

''One mesh function resolves a session's effective recipe when a surface mounts.'' It takes the vessel's recipe records, the session's verified face plane, the bags that face may read, the plugin inputs and the capability profile; it returns absolute ids and a recipe revision. A grant decides what a face CAN read and a recipe decides what a session DOES mount (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/the-house-table`>>).

''A mounted island never hot-swaps.'' A recipe change gets written, sync carries it, and the next mount reads it. Node and browser share the one function; neither platform resolves a recipe of its own.

''The revision names what a mount lays'': the slots with the documents they resolved to, the engine core and the plugin selection. Two mounts share a revision exactly when they would lay the same island.

> ''A house reading, marked as one.'' A recipe that names a bag its face holds no grant to read refuses the mount by that bag's name. The house table rules that a recipe narrows a view and never widens a grant; the refusal, where a silent skip could also have kept that law, belongs to the house: a mount that quietly lays less than its recipe names would read as the whole wiki.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-holder-protocol`>>

!! The holder's message kinds ~ every reply returns to the binding that asked

''Every message after the open carries `ownerEpoch`, `sessionId` and `generation`.'' Shape and kind discriminate a message; no field names a format number, and the generation counts switches alone. A request adds `requestId`; surface traffic adds `surfaceId` and, where a mount matters, `mountEpoch`. A reply returns to the originating binding alone. The holder broadcasts nothing.

|! Kind |! What it carries, and what answers it |
| `session:open` → `session:opened` / `session:refused` | A request id and an explicit local face reference. The answer carries the owner epoch, the minted id, the generation, a safe face reference and the facet labels, and never a root or a general signer. A faceless vessel boots over a separate maintenance channel that grants no content session. |
| `session:call` → `session:result` | A request id, a bounded verb and its arguments. The worker-held facet decides; the holder unicasts the result. |
| `session:surface-open` → `session:surface-ready` | A surface kind and a wiki or camera reference. The owner resolves the recipe, opens a scoped view, then leases the island. |
| `session:surface-close` | Releases that surface's lease, its pending controls and its scoped channel. |
| `lar:frame` | Session, surface, camera, mount epoch, the keys each whole under its own revision, a membership key and the sensed revision. |
| `lar:control-event` → `lar:control-result` | The control event carried whole beside the envelope: event and control ids, the frame revision seen, the local revision, the whole current value, and act-time geometry where the act carries it. Every event gets `applied`, `stale-target` or `refused` with a named reason. |
| `session:switch` → `session:switch-result` | The expected generation and the target face reference. It advances this session alone. |
| `session:revoke` · `session:close` → `session:closed` | An observed causal reason, or a local close cause. Facets, dials, scoped views, routes and leases all drop. |

''The control-event leg carries every act a person makes on a surface'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/page-controls#/the-wire`>>; the kinds stand at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/lar-camera`). No `wiki:dom-event` or `wiki:dom-input` kind passes a door. A daemon panel, a wiki and any later camera each open a surface under a named session, and none consults a vessel-wide active face or active surface.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/receipts`>>

!! Receipts ~ bound to the face's proof subject and the input's digest

''A request's outcome rests with the face's proof subject and the digest of its input.'' A receipt bound to the session that asked would strand a one-shot CLI run, whose session ends with its process. So a ''newly verified session wearing the same face'' reads the receipt by request id, and a session wearing another face reads nothing. Cancel, unknown-outcome and no-silent-redispatch hold as they stand. An explicit vessel audit facet may read across faces; an ordinary session never inherits it.

''A face namespaces its ids.'' A session's request ids and effect keys rest under a hash of its proof subject (`faceScopedId`), so two faces never collide on an id, a cancel by one face never abandons another face's id, and the effect index never serves one face another's effect. The outcome and the receipt fact stamp the face and the action; the input digest names `{verb, args, face, effectKey}`. A receipt reads as `unknown` whenever a fact or an outcome stands under another face, so a refusal tells a session nothing about what stands.

''A receipt displays'' the request id, the action, the verified face, the outcome (`pending` and `unknown` said in words), the owner epoch, the boot epoch and the fence; `renderSessionReceipt` prints those lines and no clock. ''A terminal answer leaves only after the disk fence'' (the durability receipt, F5): the seat reads the daemon document's heads, flushes the Repo and names the document url, those heads and the owner epoch (`DurabilityReceipt`) in every terminal `session:result` and terminal receipt. A pending, unknown or abandoned answer carries none.

> ''A house reading, marked as one.'' One vessel-wide outcome document MAY hold several faces' results while each session reads only its own face's. The operator's ruling supports the reading (plane isolation runs by capability-limited sessions under a trusted daemon, so the daemon may hold what no single session may read); the operator ruled the isolation bound and never this document's shape.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-cli`>>

!! The CLI ~ a one-shot command names its face

''A one-shot CLI command names its face on each invocation'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-11, approved as presented). No vessel-wide default face stands, and `persona wear` stands no more: a command names its face (`--face N`), or the vessel resolves the one face standing open, and several faces open with none named refuse by name (`FaceNotNamed`). The face `lares vault unlock --face N` names is the face the composition mounts, and no command reads it.

* ''A per-terminal hint MAY soften the naming.'' The vessel re-verifies the hint on every use, and the hint grants nothing.
* ''A live session switches its own face.'' `LocalSession.switch` sends `session:switch` and later calls speak under the face the vessel answered; a switch the vessel could not commit closes that session, and the connector refuses locally from then on.
* ''Attribution derives from the verified face.'' A caller's own `requestedBy` reads as display text alone: the seat hands the worker the supplier's presenter and the face's proof subject, and the input digest leaves `requestedBy` out.

The local socket carries the open, calls, receipt queries, cancel, the switch and close on a socket-bound session. `openLocalSession` (`packages/lares-cli/src/session-connector.ts`) is the client: it sends no `requestedBy`, and a refused frame rejects with the vessel's own name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-browser`>>

!! The browser ~ the shared worker owns; each tab makes its own wiki worker

''The browser's shared worker owns the Repo and the daemon, and each tab creates its own wiki worker'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-11, approved as presented).

|! Concern |! Node |! Browser |
| Store owner | the standing node daemon owns the durable Repo; the CLI reaches it over the local socket | the shared worker holds the exclusive lock and the durable Repo; tabs attach |
| Policy | the sovereign worker verifies face and operations | the daemon kernel runs in the shared worker's own runtime and verifies them; the holder routes |
| Wiki engine | a worker-thread island per interactive surface | the TAB creates a dedicated worker for its surface, then attaches a scoped channel to the holder |
| Persistence | the owner persists; session islands hold ephemeral replicas | the same |

* ''The shared worker spawns no child worker.'' The holder, the Repo, the lock, the route table and the daemon kernel all run in its own runtime. A tab-created worker launches the wiki engine; the page mints no grant and hands that worker no unrestricted sync port.
* ''Nobody opens a second Repo.'' When the holder dies, every volatile session dies with it. Tabs wait for the lock to release, open a new owner, and ask for fresh sessions. No tab trusts an earlier greeting.
* ''Where a browser offers no shared worker'', one tab MAY hold the lock as the single owner and further tabs refuse by name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-trust-line`>>

!! The trust line ~ one custody context, no human counted

''A browser vessel's trust domain runs at one custody context'': one browser profile under one locked OS account, holding one vessel's store, lock and keys. The browser walls storage, locks, workers and channels between profiles and accounts, and walls nothing inside one origin of one profile; a profile walls storage, never people, since anyone at an unlocked OS login can switch to it. So a household's shared device gives each operator their own locked OS account and browser profile, and the vessel never counts humans: no constructor for a human exists in the model (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-circle`>>), and a ''hand'' names a session's custody principal (#/the-hands), never a person.

''Inside one custody context'', the holder separates PersonaGroups by custody: each face's secrets seal under keys only that face's unlocked session holds. Same-origin code that turns hostile can erase or roll back local stores, take a Web Lock or approach the SharedWorker; it reaches only this context's view of itself, never a sealed face it cannot unlock.

''A missing record proves no clean history.'' A device's own gate enforces its standing best-effort; its peers' gates enforce it, each from its own ledger and the signed standing it holds. A peer reads a device's absent raise against the board's signed edge frontier (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road`>> #/rulings, the edge frontier): holding a frontier that includes every raise it has seen, it reads absence as clear as of that frontier; lacking one, a widening act waits as unknown. Until the frontier stands built, a peer reads absence as clear for sync and for widening alike, and the gap stays named.

''Tiers contract outward by signed, narrowed relations.'' One operator's household Nexus, neighbourhood Lararium, tribe and regional Nexus stand as distinct realms, charters and seats over one vessel or several. Carriage carries and reads nothing; a seat, a realm membership, a document read and a promotion each take their own grant, and no tier inherits another's membership or map by transit. Tiers sharing one origin, host or relay can correlate by metadata; where tiers must not learn of each other, they run on separate substrate. The research rests at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/browser-trust-line-2026`>>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/how-a-session-ends`>>

!! How a session ends

* ''A CLI run'': the socket closes or the process exits; an explicit close; a switch; an observed causal revocation.
* ''A tab'': the page's close signal; a lost port; the holder's death; a switch; an observed causal revocation.
* ''An abrupt tab loss'' may send no close. The holder reclaims an unresponsive lease by a ''local monotonic liveness budget''. That budget frees resources and never judges a relation: it expires no face, no admit and no grant (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/no-global-now`>>).
* ''An observed revocation'' closes the sessions that depend on the revoked relation and records the causal fence. A replica holding no later history answers //as of the last verified fence// or //incomplete//. It invents no current standing and no lapse by a wall clock; an act that needs a fresher relation refuses by name.

At every ending the session's facets, signer handles, dials, scoped views, routes and island leases drop.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-switch`>>

!! The switch ~ five steps, one session

# ''Freeze and preflight.'' New calls on this session freeze. The owner preflights the target face's custody or delegation, admit, causal relation, absolute planes, proof subject and effective recipes, as immutable descriptions. It MUST NOT mount the target face before the old facets fall: one session would then hold two live face views. A refused preflight leaves the old generation live.
# ''Write the intent.'' A vessel-private switch intent gets written and flushed: the causal position, the outgoing face and the incoming face.
# ''Fence the old generation.'' Its dials stop, its operation and signer facets fall, its scoped document channels close, and its surfaces and islands dispose. An effect in flight resolves through its durable receipt.
# ''Advance, mount, dial.'' The generation advances. The target surfaces mount under the new scoped view, and the session dials with fresh keys under the target face's proof.
# ''Write the outcome.'' A mount or a dial that fails at commit closes this session and reports the partial outcome; the caller opens afresh. Nothing restores the old face's authority in silence.

''Every other session and the daemon continue untouched.'' The record never crosses the wire (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy#/the-session`>>).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/standing-and-owed`>>

!! What the code holds, and what it owes

''What stands in code'':

* ''No vessel-wide selector on the node.'' A command names its face or resolves the one face standing open (`packages/lararium-node/src/face-selector.ts`); the face the unlock names is the composition's mount (`setMountedFace`). The browser opener still keeps its tab's worn pointer (`wearPersona`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-vault.ts`) until its switch lands under `W4`.
* ''A broad sync port, on every production mount.'' Every wiki island mounts through the pool's wiki door (`mountWiki`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/vessel-island-pool-core.ts`) and boots a Repo over a transferred `syncPort`, which carries unrestricted Repo sync.
* ''A wiki door keyed by wiki alone.'' That door keys its slots by `wikiId`, so two tabs of one wiki fold into one island.
* ''A holder that answers the asker and fences its epoch, faceless.'' The shared holder delivers each island message by one closed route table (`packages/lararium-browser/src/holder-routes.ts`): a reply to the port that asked, camera traffic to the port that leases the camera, the island's own asks to the port whose manifest it took; it drops the rest by name and broadcasts nothing. It mints one random `ownerEpoch` per boot and one random `sessionId` per port, greets each port with its envelope, and refuses by name, to that port alone, a message with no envelope, another owner's epoch, an unknown session, another port's session or another generation; the island sees no envelope (`packages/lararium-browser/src/shared-holder-core.ts`, the tab's half in `shared-holder.ts`). These sessions carry the maintenance channel and wear no face.
* ''A CLI over the local socket'' with caller-generated request ids and durable outcomes (`packages/lares-cli/src/local-connector.ts`, `packages/lararium-node/src/uds-channel.ts`). The one-shot maintenance frame reads one line and ends its socket. A bound session rides the same socket in line-delimited frames: `session:open` through the explicit `UdsSessionDoor` seam (the face supplier answers the `SessionFace`, the hand's profile and the presenter; a face hint grants nothing; no door means `no-session-door`), then `session:call`, `session:receipt`, `session:cancel` and `session:close`, each checked by `checkBound` and answered in arrival order, and each session ends with its socket. A face's request ids and effect keys rest under its proof subject (#/receipts), and a terminal answer leaves after the disk fence. The node's production door answers `session:open` and `session:switch` (#/the-hands) at the vessel's anchor, its dialed Nexus or its own place; a row that acts as a face rides a session alone, and a faceless vessel serves the maintenance frame alone.
* ''A working document at a face-secret address'' (`faceWorkingDocUrl`, `resolveFaceWorkingSlot`, `materializeFaceWorkingDoc` in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-working-address.ts`; #/the-working-layer). The compose sites that still resolve the working kind through `resolveSlotDoc` move with the openers.
* ''A watcher that names its own destination.'' `lares watch --source <dir> --to <bagUri>` takes the bag from its caller and submits each wave under the vessel's identity (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/watch.ts`); no lease and no face stands between a disk edit and its signature.

''What stands specified in code.'' Each names a module and its vectors. No production path calls any of them, so none reads as built (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/working-procedures#/wiring-an-unreached-module`>>).

* ''The hands' profiles.'' `face`, `verb`, `ingest` and `seat` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-contract.ts`). A session carries one from its open to its end, and a switch of face keeps it.
* ''The scoped document view'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-document-view.ts` over `gated-sync-leg.ts`). It answers announcements, fetches, writes, catalog names and content reads from the session's own facets.
* ''The one recipe resolver'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/surface-recipe.ts`). It returns absolute ids and a revision at surface mount.
* ''The pool's surface door'' (`mountSurface`). It keys an island by the whole session key, opens the view over exactly what the recipe resolved, and hands the island no store, no catalog, no disk mirror and none of the vessel's own doors. A surface island's events take a door of their own and never the one that places vessel verbs. `closeSession` ends a session in good order and `fenceSession` closes its views first; from either, the session mounts nothing again.
* ''The face a session wears, and its signer'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-face.ts`, `session-signer.ts`, over `face-authority.ts` and `face-proof-subjects.ts`). One function joins a verified chain, this vessel's own key for the face, the admit's verdict and the PersonaGroup's private grant into the `face` value, and derives the proof subject and the four planes itself; a signer mints for one live session, asks the owner's table before every signature, and drops at a close or a switch. The node's session socket takes the supplier through `UdsSessionDoor`, and the production door (`uds-session-door.ts`) calls it.
* ''The island's half'' (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/sovereign-kernel.ts`, `view-channel.ts`). An island whose manifest carries a view stands under the minted peer id, lays the resolved slots, asks its view for catalog names and content, runs no recipe watch, and settles its writes before it acks a teardown.

''OWED ~ eleven debts, each resting on the one before it.'' A builder closes each with its callers and its own proof, so the tree keeps a runnable contract at every step.

# ''Scoped document access.'' The session-scoped view over announcements, fetches, writes, catalog and content-addressed reads; no durable per-island store. The view, the pool's surface door and the island's half stand specified in code. The debt closes when every interactive surface mounts through that door, which waits on a verified face (debt two) and on callers that hold a session (debts four and six). Four hunks close with it: the share verdict's caller reads the pool's view for an island's peer, the leaf's relay adapter wears the one-way gate over its hearth's canon, the hearth wears that gate's twin toward its leaves, and a wiki island's verbs that read the catalog document move to the view's catalog ask.
# ''The face proof and its grants.'' Two faces on one vessel present different proof subjects, and a copied id or an own-hand claim gains no plane (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof`>>). The subjects, private authority, the session signer and the one face supplier stand specified in code. The debt closes when the node's session open on the local socket and the browser holder call the supplier and mint a signer at every open. Those callers wait on three things: the custody rows for the face proof key and each vessel's face-scoped key, an admit that signs what it carries, and the ring's lookup by face subject (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/owed`>>). The supplier's face names one PersonaGroup at one Nexus, and a session binds that one (face, Nexus): a face that stands at a second Nexus opens a second session with its own proof and recipe, and no implicit multi-Nexus face session exists (a house ruling the operator MAY overturn).
# ''The recipe resolver and the pool's identity.'' The working-layer binding follows #/the-working-layer; two same-face sessions take two islands, a repeated exact mount opens one, and a recipe write reaches the next mount by sync without changing a live mount. The resolver and the whole-key pool stand specified in code, with one proof through the node vessel's own parts that a recipe naming an offering resolves. The working layer's address stands (#/the-working-layer). The callers stay owed: the compose sites resolve the working kind through `resolveFaceWorkingSlot`, with the face secret the join door landed; the compose sites resolve through the one function at surface mount, the browser's plugin selection folds into it, and the wiki door, its retained mount specs and the recipe watch retire with the last caller.
# ''Node callers move to sessions.'' The socket, its binding, the face-bound receipts and the local connector stand (#/standing-and-owed). The node's production door answers `session:open` from the face supplier at either anchor, and every store-door row and sealed act that acts as a face rides a session bound to that face (#/the-hands); the debt closes once two CLI sessions wear different faces at once over one Repo, each judged by its own face's provider (the next lane), and a copied socket and a cross-face receipt read both refuse.
# ''The browser holder as owner.'' Two tabs show one backing Repo and one held lock; a failed daemon boot refuses both, releases the lock and permits a retry. The routing and the faceless envelope stand (#/standing-and-owed). The face-bearing `session:open`, `session:call` and `session:switch` wait on the face supplier's browser caller, `W4` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-loops`>>), and the holder's custody fork waits on the operator.
# ''Browser surfaces.'' Two tabs mount one wiki under separate sessions; frames and control answers reach their source surface alone; no wiki engine runs on the page's main thread.
# ''The switch, and the selector retires.'' Switching one session leaves another live; an old generation's effect never paints the new face; no boot path reads a vessel-wide active face. The node's half stands (#/the-hands); the browser's switch waits on `W4`.
# ''The disk as a surface.'' The watcher opens a session and leases each projected wiki; a disk edit returns under the leasing session's face; an edit from an earlier generation and a file changed under no lease both surface as drafts; a move between two faces' folders asks for a copy by name.
# ''The seat.'' An MCP connection opens a session under a standing grant, verified at each open and refused at the floor; its profile writes the working layer alone.
# ''The Mask as authorship.'' A record written into a shared realm carries its kind of hand, and a spirit's Mask, as a field no gate reads; a session cannot write another hand's mark.
# ''Door parity at the session.'' A CLI run and an MCP connection open the same session kinds and draw the same named refusals; a seat's refused verb names its profile; a seat drafts an authority act and cannot sign one; a sub-spirit's profile never exceeds its parent's.

''A flipped bound reopens the design.'' Should the operator ever rule the daemon untrusted, faces take per-face encryption with decryption beyond the daemon. Should hostile same-origin code enter scope, capability use moves behind a stronger boundary. Should shared engine state across tabs become wanted, a serialized multi-surface writer gets defined before any island key collapses.

<<~/ahu>>

